Fixes #1350 

I fixed a bug in UNET (#1350) where `this.video` was not being handled properly.  Instead of copy and pasting the logic from another model, I moved it into a utility function.

That allows us to remove repetitive chunks of code like this from a bunch of models:
```
await tf.nextFrame();

if (this.video && this.video.readyState === 0) {
  await new Promise(resolve => {
    this.video.onloadeddata = () => resolve();
  });
}
```

Utility is used in:

- [x] BodyPix
- [x] FaceApi
- [x] FaceMesh
- [x] Handpose 
- [x] ImageClassifier
- [x] PoseNet
- [x] UNET

Next up: fix the models which rely on the `Video` class which doesn't work in Safari (#626)
